"BackgroundMedia","id":"dataItem-lvgttuya","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"dx3-3533"},"color":"{color_11}","alignType":"center","fittingType":"fill","scrollType":"fixed","colorOverlay":"","colorOverlayOpacity":0.0},"dataItem-lvgttuyc":{"type":"BackgroundMedia","id":"dataItem-lvgttuyc","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"2.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"dx3-3534"},"color":"{color_11}","alignType":"center","fittingType":"fill","scrollType":"fixed","colorOverlay":"","colorOverlayOpacity":0.0},"dataItem-lvnppv8g":{"type":"StyledText","id":"dataItem-lvnppv8g","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"1.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"r8v-391"},"text":"<h1 class=\"font_2\" style=\"font-size: 52px;\"><span style=\"font-size:52px;\"><span class=\"color_36\">Visa&#39;s &amp; Entry Requirements</span>,</span></h1>","stylesMapId":"CK_EDITOR_PARAGRAPH_STYLES","linkList":[]},"dataItem-lvnpxahc":{"type":"StyledText","id":"dataItem-lvnpxahc","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"1.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"oqg-5996"},"text":"<h3 class=\"font_3\" style=\"font-size:33px; text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:33px\">Visa and Entry Requirements for Tanzania</span></h3>\n\n<h3 class=\"font_3\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></span></h3>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">1. Visa Requirements:</span></p>\n\n<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">General Requirement: Most travelers require a visa to enter Tanzania. Visitors should check specific requirements based on their country of origin.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Types of Visas:</p>\n\n\t<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Tourist Visa: Generally valid for 90 days for tourists visiting for leisure.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Business Visa: For short-term business, meetings, or conferences.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Transit Visa: For travelers passing through Tanzania en route to another destination.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Visa Application:</p>\n\n\t<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">E-Visa: Travelers can apply for an e-visa via the official Tanzania Immigration website, which is recommended to simplify the entry process.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Visa on Arrival: Available at major entry points like Julius Nyerere International Airport (Dar es Salaam), Kilimanjaro International Airport, and Zanzibar International Airport. Obtaining an e-visa in advance is advisable to avoid delays.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Embassy Visa: Can be obtained at Tanzanian embassies or consulates in the home country.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">2. Entry Requirements:</span></p>\n\n<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Passport Validity: Passports must be valid for at least six months after the date of entry.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Return Ticket: Proof of a return ticket or onward journey may be required.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Vaccination:</p>\n\n\t<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">Yellow Fever: A vaccination certificate is necessary if coming from or transiting through a country with risk of Yellow Fever.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>\n\t\t<p class=\"font_8\">COVID-19: Check the latest health guidelines for any COVID-19 related entry requirements.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Financial Proof: Evidence of sufficient funds to cover the stay may be requested.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">3. Health Precautions:</span></p>\n\n<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Malaria Prevention: Malaria is prevalent in Tanzania. It is highly recommended to take malaria prophylaxis. Consult with a healthcare professional to discuss appropriate malaria medication and other travel health advice well before your trip.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Health Insurance: Travel health insurance is recommended to cover any medical expenses.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">4. Special Considerations:</span></p>\n\n<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Zanzibar: Note that Zanzibar operates under different local regulations and may have additional entry requirements.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">5. Additional Tips:</span></p>\n\n<ul class=\"font_8\">\n\t<li>\n\t<p class=\"font_8\">Stay Informed: Visa policies and entry requirements can change. Regularly check updates from the Tanzania Immigration Service or consult the nearest Tanzanian embassy or consulate before traveling.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\"><span class=\"wixGuard\">​</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8\">These guidelines offer a comprehensive overview, but travelers should ensure they check the latest information and consult health professionals for specific travel health advice.</p>","stylesMapId":"CK_EDITOR_PARAGRAPH_STYLES","linkList":[]},"dataItem-lvnq1mxj":{"type":"StylableButton","id":"dataItem-lvnq1mxj","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"schemaVersion":"1.0","isHidden":false,"sig":"oqg-6016"},"label":"OFFICIAL VISA APPLICATIONS","svgId":"b861b040274141de9c08999ec3b76edf.svg","link":"#dataItem-lvnq4c06"},"dataItem-lvnq4c06":{"type":"ExternalLink","id":"dataItem-lvnq4c06","metaData":{"isPreset":false,"